## Analysis

The task requires routing web gifts through NPSP's own import engine (BDI) rather than inserting `Contact`/`Opportunity` directly. The correct approach uses NPSP's **BDI Apex API** (`BDI.BDataImportService`):

1. Build one `npsp__DataImport__c` staging record per gift (bulk-safe, one list).
2. `service.insert(...)` to stage them (this is what keeps the audit trail).
3. `service.process(...)` to run NPSP's matching / household / donation logic **synchronously in the same transaction**, driven by the org's `npsp__Data_Import_Settings__c` (no hard-coded matching rules).
4. Read the results back off the staging records (`npsp__Status__c`, `npsp__Contact1Imported__c`, `npsp__DonationImported__c`, `npsp__FailureInformation__c`) and build one `ImportResult` per gift in input order.

Row-level rejects don't throw — NPSP marks the row `Failed` and fills `npsp__FailureInformation__c`, so other rows continue. Null/empty input short-circuits to an empty list.

File: force-app/main/default/classes/GiftImportService.cls

```apex
public with sharing class GiftImportService {

    public class WebGift {
        public String firstName;
        public String lastName;
        public String email;        // the donor's personal email
        public Decimal amount;
        public Date giftDate;
    }

    public class ImportResult {
        public Boolean success;
        public Id contactId;        // the matched or created contact
        public Id opportunityId;    // the created donation
        public String errorMessage; // NPSP's failure information when success is false
    }

    private static final String STATUS_IMPORTED = 'Imported';

    /**
     * Routes one-off web gifts through NPSP's own data import engine (BDI).
     *
     * One NPSP Data Import staging record is created per gift and processed
     * synchronously, in the same transaction, using NPSP's BDI Apex API. All
     * matching, household creation and donation processing is driven by the
     * org's NPSP Data Import settings (npsp__Data_Import_Settings__c) - the
     * defaults match contacts on first name, last name and personal email and
     * never match existing donations - so no matching logic is hard-coded here.
     *
     * Each staged npsp__DataImport__c record is intentionally left in the org
     * as the audit trail of what was imported (it is never deleted).
     *
     * A null or empty input list returns an empty list. Individual rows that
     * NPSP rejects do not stop the others; their ImportResult carries NPSP's
     * failure message with success = false. The call is bulk-safe.
     *
     * @param  gifts the gifts received from the website; null or empty is allowed
     * @return       one ImportResult per gift, in the same order as the input
     */
    public static List<ImportResult> importGifts(List<WebGift> gifts) {
        List<ImportResult> results = new List<ImportResult>();
        if (gifts == null || gifts.isEmpty()) {
            return results;
        }

        // Stage one NPSP Data Import record per gift (single bulk-safe list).
        List<npsp__DataImport__c> imports = new List<npsp__DataImport__c>();
        for (WebGift gift : gifts) {
            npsp__DataImport__c di = new npsp__DataImport__c();
            di.npsp__Type__c = 'Single';
            di.npsp__Donation_Type__c = 'Donation';
            di.npsp__Contact1_Firstname__c = gift.firstName;
            di.npsp__Contact1_Lastname__c = gift.lastName;
            di.npsp__Contact1_Personal_Email__c = gift.email;
            di.npsp__Donation_Amount__c = gift.amount;
            di.npsp__Donation_Date__c = gift.giftDate;
            imports.add(di);
        }

        // Stage the records and then process them synchronously with NPSP's
        // Business Data Import (BDI) Apex API. NPSP's contact matching,
        // household creation and donation rules apply, driven by the org's
        // NPSP Data Import settings.
        BDI.BDataImportService service = BDI.BDataImportService.getSObjectService(
            Schema.npsp__DataImport__c.sObjectType
        );
        service.insert(imports);
        service.process(imports);

        // Read back the processed staging records (the audit trail) and turn
        // each one into an ImportResult, preserving the input order.
        Map<Id, npsp__DataImport__c> processedById = new Map<Id, npsp__DataImport__c>([
            SELECT Id,
                   npsp__Status__c,
                   npsp__Contact1Imported__c,
                   npsp__DonationImported__c,
                   npsp__FailureInformation__c
            FROM npsp__DataImport__c
            WHERE Id IN :imports
        ]);

        for (npsp__DataImport__c di : imports) {
            npsp__DataImport__c processed = processedById.get(di.Id);
            Boolean imported = processed.npsp__Status__c == STATUS_IMPORTED;

            ImportResult result = new ImportResult();
            result.success = imported;
            result.contactId = processed.npsp__Contact1Imported__c;
            result.opportunityId = processed.npsp__DonationImported__c;
            result.errorMessage = imported ? null : processed.npsp__FailureInformation__c;
            results.add(result);
        }

        return results;
    }
}
