## Reasoning

The compile failures all trace back to one root cause: I referenced `Schema.SObjectDescribeResult`, which is **not** a valid Apex type. The correct object-describe return type is `Schema.DescribeSObjectResult`, but rather than name these types at all (which is what caused the cascade of spurious downstream errors), I'll inline the describe calls.

Key fixes:
- `FB_Employee__c.getDescribe().isReadable()` — object-level guard, no explicit describe type needed.
- `FB_Employee__c.<Field>__c.getDescribe().isReadable()` — `SObjectField.getDescribe()` returns `DescribeFieldResult`, whose `isReadable()` method is valid; inlining avoids any type-name resolution issues.
- Dynamic SOQL only selects fields the user can read, so unreadable fields are genuinely **absent** (not null) from the returned sObjects.
- `with sharing` still enforces record-level sharing on the dynamic query.

File: force-app/main/default/classes/EmployeeDirectoryService.cls
```apex
public with sharing class EmployeeDirectoryService {

    /**
     * Returns the FB_Employee__c records the running user can see through
     * sharing rules (record-level sharing is NOT bypassed), ordered by Name
     * ascending.
     *
     * Field-level security is enforced: any of the sensitive custom fields
     * (Department__c, Salary__c, Personal_Email__c) that the running user
     * cannot read are omitted from the SELECT clause entirely, so they are
     * absent from the returned records rather than present with a null value.
     * The method never throws because of FLS; a user who can read only some of
     * those fields still gets the records with the fields they can read.
     *
     * @return List of FB_Employee__c containing only the fields the running
     *         user can read. An empty list is returned when the running user
     *         cannot read the object at all.
     */
    public static List<FB_Employee__c> getDirectory() {
        // Object-level guard: if the running user cannot read the object at
        // all, return an empty list instead of letting the query throw.
        if (!FB_Employee__c.getDescribe().isReadable()) {
            return new List<FB_Employee__c>();
        }

        // Id and Name are always included.
        List<String> fields = new List<String>{ 'Id', 'Name' };

        // Only query the custom fields the running user can read, so that
        // unreadable fields are absent (not merely null) in the results.
        if (FB_Employee__c.Department__c.getDescribe().isReadable()) {
            fields.add('Department__c');
        }
        if (FB_Employee__c.Salary__c.getDescribe().isReadable()) {
            fields.add('Salary__c');
        }
        if (FB_Employee__c.Personal_Email__c.getDescribe().isReadable()) {
            fields.add('Personal_Email__c');
        }

        // Because the class is declared "with sharing", this dynamic query
        // still honors the running user's record-level sharing settings.
        String soql = 'SELECT ' + String.join(fields, ', ')
                      + ' FROM FB_Employee__c ORDER BY Name ASC';

        return Database.query(soql);
    }
}
```

